      },
      "message": "fix(post): engage cutter compensation in G17, never in a stale G18/G19\n\nA G41/G42/G40 block that followed an XZ/YZ arc was written while\nG18/G19 was still modal, so the control compensated in that plane\ninstead of XY. The Fanuc, Haas, Mazak and Siemens 840D posts now state\nG17 on the comp block when the modal plane is not 17, and refuse by\nname an XZ/YZ arc while compensation is engaged (no plane switch under\ncomp). Programs that never leave G17 post byte-identically.\n\nPinned by crates/post/tests/comp_plane.rs.\n\nFixes #391\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
